Design notes:

- P1 traffic: every frame is copied to P3. Intra-segment IPv4 (10.0.2.0/24 to 10.0.2.0/24) and ARP are also sent to P2. All other P1 frames go to P3 only.
- P3 traffic: all frames are returned to P1.
- P2 traffic: IPv4 to the segment (dst 10.0.2.0/24) and ARP go to P1. Everything else is dropped by the default rule.

The prompt does not say the P2 to P1 traffic must also be copied to the tap, so I send it to P1 only.

```json
[
  {
    "id": "p1-ipv4-intra",
    "priority": 300,
    "outputPorts": [2, 3],
    "match": {
      "inPort": 1,
      "etherType": 2048,
      "srcIp": "10.0.2.0",
      "srcIpPrefixLen": 24,
      "dstIp": "10.0.2.0",
      "dstIpPrefixLen": 24
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "p1-arp",
    "priority": 300,
    "outputPorts": [2, 3],
    "match": {
      "inPort": 1,
      "etherType": 2054
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "p1-other-to-tap",
    "priority": 100,
    "outputPorts": [3],
    "match": {
      "inPort": 1
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "tap-to-p1",
    "priority": 200,
    "outputPorts": [1],
    "match": {
      "inPort": 3
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "uplink-ipv4-to-segment",
    "priority": 300,
    "outputPorts": [1],
    "match": {
      "inPort": 2,
      "etherType": 2048,
      "dstIp": "10.0.2.0",
      "dstIpPrefixLen": 24
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "uplink-arp-to-p1",
    "priority": 300,
    "outputPorts": [1],
    "match": {
      "inPort": 2,
      "etherType": 2054
    }
  }
]
